#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1363 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "NEW with the M2-P9 ruling (option (b) / M2-D29, Fix #307) - the FDA mirror of pmda/PMDA-SD1363/PMDA-SD1363-invalid_screening_not_completed-DM.cdt. FDA-SD1363's Check is byte-identical to PMDA-SD1363's and its sheet row carries the same sentence, so the fifth ARMNULRS term ('SCREENING NOT COMPLETED', SDTM CT C142179, added 2025-09-26) travels to both or the twin group acquires a divergence it did not have. Row 2 is the conformant control."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 ARMCD=A
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
col ARMNRS  type=Char label="Reason Arm and/or Actual Arm is Null"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 | A | Arm A | SCREENING NOT COMPLETED
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023 |   |       | SCREEN FAILURE
